Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Task status change: ask for a note, with a title filled
 in
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Changing a task's status (the status menu on a lead or deal, dragging a card
on the Tasks board, or editing the task) opens a dialog asking for a note
about the change. The note can be skipped; cancelling leaves the status as it
was. The title is filled in from the change ("Done: Follow up · 7d late",
"Reopened: ...", "Started: ...") so notes read by outcome in the Notes list.

Once the note has some text, an app can suggest a better title through the
crm_task_note_title server hook (crm.api.task.suggest_note_title). It is
requested a second after typing stops, only replaces a title the person has
not edited, and falls back to the filled-in one when there is no hook, an
error, or a slow answer.

- utils/taskNoteTitle.js: the pure title formula
- TaskStatusNoteModal and promptTaskStatusNote(): the dialog and a promise
  for it; the task dialog shows its own copy, nested, to share its focus
- AllModals, ViewControls and DoctypeModal: the three places a status changes
- TextEditorControl: also emits `input` on every edit

Modified by Másquetú, 2026-11-26.

